<title>USA: TENNECO TO BUY MEXICAN CATALYTIC CONVERTER MAKER.</title>
<headline>TENNECO TO BUY MEXICAN CATALYTIC CONVERTER MAKER.</headline>
<dateline>DEERFIELD, Ill. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tenneco Inc's Tenneco Automotive unit said Thursday it has reached agreement to buy Autocan, a Mexican catalytic converter and exhaust pipe assembly manufacturer. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Located in Puebla, Mexico, Autocan currently supplies catalytic converters and &quot;downpipe&quot; exhaust assemblies for Volkswagen, the largest passenger car producer in that country, as well as for Chrysler and BMW.</p>
<p>Anticipated 1997 sales for Autocan are $25 million, Tenneco Automotive said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
